      explanation: `<div style="--mx-navy:#01506e; --mx-blue:#207bb5; --mx-lightblue:#0099d4; --mx-yellow:#e9dc12; --mx-grey:#4B556A; --mx-rule:#dde4ea; --mx-tint:#f2f7fa; --mx-body:#232a33; color:var(--mx-body); line-height:1.6"><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-yellow); padding:13px 18px; margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">A. A debit to bond discount of $1,000 is correct.</strong> The bonds sold for $49,000 but must be carried at a $50,000 face obligation, so the $1,000 shortfall is debited to discount.</div><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The rule</h3><p style="margin:0 0 12px">A bond quote is a <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">percentage of face value</strong>. A price of 98 means the investor pays 98% of maturity value. Bonds payable is always credited at <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">face amount</strong>, because that is the legal obligation at maturity, no matter what cash comes in.</p><p style="margin:0 0 18px">Cash below face creates a <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">discount</strong>, a contra-liability with a <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">debit</strong> balance that reduces carrying value. Cash above face creates a <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">premium</strong>, a credit balance. The discount is <strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">amortized</strong> over the bond life, pushing interest expense above the cash coupon because the effective rate exceeds the stated rate.</p><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The math</h3><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-blue); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:18px"><table style="border:0; border-collapse:collapse; width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Maturity value</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$50,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Issue price, $50,000 x 98%</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$49,000</td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Discount</strong></td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">$1,000</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">The entry at issuance</h3><div style="background:var(--mx-tint); border-left:4px solid var(--mx-blue); padding:8px 10px; margin-bottom:18px"><table style="border:0; border-collapse:collapse; width:100%"><tbody><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Account</strong></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Debit</strong></td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">Credit</strong></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Cash</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$49,000</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px">Discount on bonds payable</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$1,000</td><td style="border:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--mx-rule); padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td></tr><tr><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px 11px 40px">Bonds payable</td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right"></td><td style="border:0; padding:11px 14px; text-align:right">$50,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 style="color:var(--mx-navy); font-size:17px; margin:0 0 8px">Why the others are wrong</h3><p style="margin:0; color:var(--mx-grey)"><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">B.</strong> Credits bonds payable at the net proceeds, but the liability is recorded at the $50,000 face amount.<br /><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">C.</strong> Reverses the direction: a price below 100 is a discount, and a premium would carry a credit balance.<br /><strong style="color:var(--mx-navy)">D.</strong> Debiting bonds payable would retire the debt, not issue it.</p></div>`,
